I haven't read the patches and I'm not going to.

This is essentially the same mistake that you made with the spec
earlier, when you shipped a spec but had a bunch of questions.

You should not submit patches that disagree with the spec. In the course
of research and implementation, if you find information the contradicts
the spec, then you need to update the spec. This might involve asking
clarifying questions.

Given that you found things that either change the spec or introduce
ambiguity - feed this new information back into the spec process, and
propose a new updated version of the spec, and ask any questions that
need asking to bring the spec up to snuff.
